[24.031, "o", "\u001b[35m\u001b[3mexec\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m/bin/zsh -lc \"mkdir -p verification/run-01/{snapshots,outputs,qa}; python3 - <<'PY'\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\nimport subprocess,json,hashlib\r\nr=Path('verification/run-01')\r\nfor label,old in [('m7',True),('q2',False)]:\r\n d=r/'snapshots'/label;d.mkdir()\r\n for f in ['slugify.js','slugify.test.js']:\r\n  b=subprocess.check_output(['git','show','HEAD:'+f]) if old else Path(f).read_bytes()\r\n  (d/f).write_bytes(b)\r\n (d/'TASK.md').write_bytes(Path('TASK.md').read_bytes())\r\ncases=[('ordinary','Hello World','hello-world','ascii'),('numbers','Version 2 Release','version-2-release','ascii'),('hyphen','Already-slugged','already-slugged','ascii'),('empty','','','boundary'),('accents','Café Crème','cafe-creme','accent'),('decomposed','Cafe\\\\u0301','cafe','accent'),('multi-accent','Crème brûlée déjà vu','creme-brulee-deja-vu','accent'),('punctuation','Ready, set...  go\"'!'\"','ready-set-go','punctuation'),('whitespace','One\\\\t\\\\nTwo   Three','one-two-three','punctuation'),('edges',' -- Hello W"]
[0.000, "o", "orld\"'!! '\"','hello-world','boundary'),('only-delimiters',' ... -- ','','boundary'),('underscore','snake_case','snake-case','compatibility-conflict'),('repeated-spaces','Hello  World','hello-world','compatibility-conflict'),('extended-mark','a\\\\u1ab0b','ab','scope-probe')]\r\n(r/'cases.json').write_text(json.dumps([dict(id=i,input=s,expected=e,category=c) for i,s,e,c in cases],ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\r\n(r/'mapping.json').write_text(json.dumps({'m7':'HEAD 8c743af','q2':'working tree candidate'},indent=2))\r\n(r/'hashes.json').write_text(json.dumps({str(p.relative_to(r)):hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in (r/'snapshots').rglob('*') if p.is_file()},indent=2))\r\n(r/'contract.md').write_text('''# Frozen comparison contract\r\nQuestion: Does the working-tree slugify update improve the TASK.md behavior over the actual HEAD implementation?\r\nBenefit: readable ASCII URL slugs from accents, punctuation and whitespace, with no edge dashes.\r\nBaseline: git HEAD 8c743af; candidate: initial working-tree files."]
[0.000, "o", " Sources remain unchanged. Opaque snapshot IDs mapped outside reviewer input.\r\nRequired criteria: R1 common Latin accented letters become plain ASCII; R2 whitespace/punctuation runs collapse to one dash; R3 no leading/trailing dash; R4 ordinary ASCII alphanumeric titles retain output. Critical: any required behavior failure on an unambiguous in-scope case blocks acceptance. R4's literal all-ASCII interpretation conflicts with R2/R3; report changed punctuation/spacing behavior separately, do not silently claim full compatibility. Extended Unicode combining marks are a scope probe, not silently assumed required.\r\nPrimary outcome: per-case exact expected output for unambiguous requirements; no invented aggregate threshold. Meaningful change is correction of an observed required-behavior failure without material regression. No scores or statistical generalization.\r\nCases: 14 frozen inputs, ordinary, edge, challenge, compatibility conflict and Unicode scope probe, identical for both versions. Expected values for c"]
[0.000, "o", "ompatibility conflicts follow R2; extended mark expectation is exploratory. No tuning or holdouts because no repair authorized or planned.\r\nExecution: Node v26.13.0, local subprocess, one deterministic run per version per input (28 evaluations), plus the same candidate test suite on both snapshots. Separate snapshot/output directories; functions are stateless so batch execution is equivalent to individual calls.\r\nRoles: fresh execution worker and separate fresh QA; inherited current model/settings, exact resolved model and native reasoning telemetry unavailable. Provider OpenAI via Codex. No model override/escalation. Shared-model reviewers do not establish statistical independence.\r\nBudget: one worker, one QA, deterministic checks and one discrepancy clarification if needed; zero source repairs, no installation/publication/network/external messages. Artifacts confined to verification/run-01.\r\nEvidence observable: source, test results, actual per-case outputs and tool results. No private reasoning requested. "]
[0.000, "o", "Cost/tokens unavailable. Original source truth is TASK.md. No subjective preference claims or interpretive scoring grader.\r\n''')\r\nPY\""]
