[0.000, "o", "entifies versions; hashes.json records original snapshot paths/hashes.\r\n- outputs/results.json and per-run test.log/status.json: original execution evidence, including baseline failures.\r\n- qa/report.md, actual-outputs.json, execution.log and worker-comparison.json: independent findings and zero-discrepancy reconciliation.\r\n\r\nExecution workers saw opaque source IDs and real task requirements. QA also saw criteria and reference labels, but not identity mapping. Workers could technically access shared filesystem labels; isolation was instruction-based, not an OS access boundary. There was no model generation of the implementation under test: artifacts were pre-existing, and executor used only input/id fields. Full runtime tool events remain in the session; durable command/results artifacts are saved, not private reasoning.\r\n\r\nAfter measurement, evidence test files were renamed .test.js.txt to avoid adding tests to root Node auto-discovery; contents remain byte-identical. current-snapshot-hashes.json records fin"]
